<title>FINLAND: Amer opens up after K-share buyback news.</title>
<headline>Amer opens up after K-share buyback news.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish sporting goods group Amer-Yhtyma opened up 8.00 markka at 100.00 on Tuesday and then retreated slightly after the company said it would redeem 275,000 of its K-shares.</p>
<p>At 1355/1055 GMT, Amer traded at 96.00, up 4.70 markka or more than five percent. It had been suspended all session pending the announcement.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 24x</p>
